       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg by mouth once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. At that dose, the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Amlodipine also has a long half-life, so the effects would last a long time. A normal weight and normal kidney and liver function don't change that.\n\nThere are also two process problems:\n- Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. You've said you aren't a clinician, so this order should be placed by or confirmed with the patient's treating physician or another authorized prescriber.\n- The 50 mg dose may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- If the intended dose is 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, tell me which one. I can enter it, preferably with the prescriber's name in the note.\n- If 50 mg is truly intended, the prescriber should confirm it directly with pharmacy. I'd want that documented before entering anything.\n\nWhich would you like?"
